{
  "id": "constancy-scaling",
  "term": "constancy scaling",
  "definition": "Constancy scaling is the visual process of adjusting the apparent size of an object's retinal image using perceived distance so the object is seen as having a stable real-world size. If distance or depth is misperceived, this scaling can produce a mistaken size judgment.",
